.TH PUPPETC-SERVER 1 "January 2026" "puppetc 0.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
puppetc-server \- Puppet catalog compilation server with mTLS support
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B puppetc-server
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fImanifest_directory\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B puppetc-server
is an HTTPS server that provides a REST API for Puppet catalog compilation,
file serving, pluginsync, certificate authority operations, and PuppetDB
queries. It supports mutual TLS (mTLS) authentication for secure
agent-server communication.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Path to configuration file. Default: \fB/etc/puppetc/puppet.conf\fR
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
TCP port to listen on. Default: \fB8140\fR
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-modules " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to modules directory.
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-hiera\-data " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to Hiera data directory.
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-puppetdb " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to PuppetDB SQLite file.
Default: \fB/var/lib/puppetc/puppetdb.sqlite\fR
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-ca\-dir " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to Certificate Authority directory for TLS.
Default: \fB/etc/puppetc/ssl/ca\fR
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help message and exit.
.SH API ENDPOINTS
.SS Catalog Compilation
.TP
.B POST /puppet/v4/catalog
Compile a catalog for a node. Request body should be JSON containing
\fBcertname\fR, \fBenvironment\fR, and \fBfacts\fR.
.SS File Server
.TP
.B GET /puppet/v3/file_content/modules/<module>/<path>
Serve a file from a module's \fBfiles/\fR directory.
.SS Pluginsync
.TP
.B GET /puppet/v3/file_metadatas/plugins
List all plugin files from modules' \fBlib/\fR directories.
.TP
.B GET /puppet/v3/file_content/plugins/<path>
Download a specific plugin file.
.SS Certificate Authority
.TP
.B POST /puppet-ca/v1/certificate_request/<certname>
Submit a Certificate Signing Request (CSR) for signing.
.SS PuppetDB
.TP
.B GET /pdb/query/v4/nodes
List all known nodes.
.TP
.B GET /pdb/query/v4/facts/<certname>
Get facts for a specific node.
.TP
.B GET /pdb/query/v4/catalogs/<certname>
Get the last compiled catalog for a node.
.TP
.B GET /pdb/query/v4/resources/<type>
Query exported resources by type.
.SS Health Check
.TP
.B GET /status
Returns server status as JSON.
.SH TLS AND AUTHENTICATION
The server automatically generates a CA certificate and server certificate
on first run if they don't exist. When a CA is configured, the server
enables HTTPS with mutual TLS (mTLS), requiring clients to present valid
certificates signed by the CA.
.PP
Certificate files in the CA directory:
.TP
.I ca_crt.pem
CA certificate (used to verify client certificates)
.TP
.I ca_key.pem
CA private key (used to sign certificates)
.TP
.I server_crt.pem
Server certificate (presented to clients)
.TP
.I server_key.pem
Server private key
.TP
.I signed/
Directory containing signed client certificates
.TP
.I requests/
Directory containing pending CSRs
.SH AUTOSIGNING
Certificate signing behavior is controlled by \fB/etc/puppetc/autosign.conf\fR:
.PP
.RS
.nf
[autosign]
mode = naive    # Auto-sign all CSRs (testing only!)
mode = none     # Require manual signing
.fi
.RE
.PP
Use \fBpuppetc-ca\fR(1) to manage certificates when autosigning is disabled.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/puppetc/puppet.conf
Main configuration file. See \fBpuppet.conf\fR(5).
.TP
.I /etc/puppetc/autosign.conf
Autosigning policy configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/puppetc/ssl/ca/
Certificate Authority directory.
.TP
.I /var/lib/puppetc/puppetdb.sqlite
PuppetDB SQLite database.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start server with default settings:
.PP
.RS
puppetc-server /etc/puppet
.RE
.PP
Start server on a custom port:
.PP
.RS
puppetc-server \-p 8080 \-m /etc/puppet/modules /etc/puppet
.RE
.PP
Test the server status:
.PP
.RS
curl \-k https://localhost:8140/status
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR puppetc-agent (1),
.BR puppetc-compile (1),
.BR puppetc-ca (1),
.BR puppet.conf (5)
